abstract: >-
  This repository contains a sequential hybrid simulation
  model for examining the relationship between
  musculoskeletal clinical need, referral access, patient
  pathways, and service capacity in elective Trauma and
  Orthopaedics. A System Dynamics component represents
  changes in population-level demand and severity, while a
  Discrete-Event Simulation component models the subsequent
  progression of individual patients through
  resource-constrained services. Patient routing is informed
  by Probabilistic Deterministic Finite Automata learned
  from historical pathways. The model supports the
  evaluation of alternative deterioration, gatekeeping,
  referral, and capacity assumptions, with outputs including
  referral volumes, waiting times, queueing, pathway
  completion, and resource use.
